---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/urls';
const privacySections = [
  { id: 'scope', label: 'Scope' },
  { id: 'game-data', label: 'Game data' },
  { id: 'advertising-diagnostics', label: 'Advertising and diagnostics' },
  { id: 'information-you-provide', label: 'Information you provide' },
  { id: 'website-operation', label: 'Website operation' },
  { id: 'sharing-retention', label: 'Sharing and retention' },
  { id: 'choices', label: 'Your choices' },
  { id: 'security', label: 'Security' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Changes and contact' },
] as const;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How US5 Incorporation and Neon Bubble Galaxy handle information."
  path="/privacy/"
  updated="29 August 2026"
  sections={privacySections}
  ><h2 id="scope">Scope</h2><p>
    This policy covers the US5 Incorporation corporate website and the mobile game <strong
      >Neon Bubble Galaxy</strong
    >. It explains what US5 handles directly and what our third-party service providers process when
    you use the game.
  </p><div class="app-privacy-card">
    <img
      src={withBase('/images/neon-bubble-galaxy.png')}
      alt="Neon Bubble Galaxy game icon"
      width="512"
      height="512"
    /><div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Mobile game</span><h2 id="game-data">Neon Bubble Galaxy</h2><p>
        Neon Bubble Galaxy does not require an account. US5 does not directly collect your name,
        email address, contacts, precise location, photos, or gameplay content through the game. US5
        does not sell personal data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div><h2 id="advertising-diagnostics">Advertising and diagnostics in the game</h2><p>
    Neon Bubble Galaxy uses the <strong>Google Mobile Ads SDK (AdMob)</strong> to provide advertising.
    Google states that this SDK automatically collects and shares IP address, user interactions with the
    app, diagnostic information, and device or account identifiers for advertising, analytics, and fraud
    prevention. Advertising may be personalized or non-personalized depending on consent, age, region,
    device settings, and the app's configuration.
  </p><p>
    The game also uses <strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong> to identify crashes and improve stability.
    Crashlytics may automatically process crash logs, app and device diagnostics, and installation identifiers.
    This information is used to investigate errors, prevent failures, and maintain the game.
  </p><p>
    These services are provided by Google and operate under <a
      href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a
    >. Their automatic SDK processing means it would not be accurate to say that no data is
    processed or shared when the game is used.
  </p><h2 id="information-you-provide">Information you choose to provide</h2><p>
    This website does not receive or store form submissions. The enquiry form prepares a message in
    your own email application. If you send it, US5 Incorporation receives the information through
    email and uses it to respond and manage the resulting correspondence.
  </p><h2 id="website-operation">Website operation</h2><p>
    We do not intentionally deploy analytics, advertising, accounts, or non-essential cookies.
    GitHub Pages delivers the website and may process ordinary technical information such as IP
    addresses and request logs under GitHub’s own terms and privacy practices.
  </p><h2 id="sharing-retention">Sharing and retention</h2><p>
    US5 does not sell personal data. We do not independently share information for unrelated
    purposes. Google processes the game data described above as our advertising and diagnostics
    provider. Email and infrastructure providers process information as needed to deliver their
    services. Google controls retention within AdMob and Crashlytics under its policies and service
    settings. We retain correspondence only while relevant to support, security, legal, or
    legitimate record-keeping needs, then remove it when no longer reasonably needed.
  </p><h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2><p>
    You can manage advertising choices through your device and Google settings. You may also reset
    or delete your device's advertising identifier and uninstall the game. You may contact us to ask
    about, correct, or request deletion of information held in correspondence, subject to
    information we reasonably need to retain for security, legal, or record-keeping purposes. The
    game has no US5 account or saved profile to delete.
  </p><h2 id="security">Security</h2><p>
    We use reasonable care when handling correspondence, but no internet transmission or storage
    method can be guaranteed completely secure.
  </p><h2 id="contact">Changes and contact</h2><p>
    We may update this policy when the website, game, or service providers change. Questions and
    privacy requests can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.
  </p></LegalLayout
>

<style>
  .app-privacy-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8rem 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: var(--paper);
  }
  .app-privacy-card img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
  }
  .app-privacy-card h2,
  .app-privacy-card p {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .app-privacy-card {
      grid-template-columns: 5rem 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
